  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg">
        <tei:pb ed="1965" n="4" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg"/>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/adon_olam"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>Lord of the world, He who has reigned before any form was created. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/leet_naasah"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>At the time when by His will everything came into being, then was His Name proclaimed as King. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/veacharei"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>And after everything ceases to be then He alone inspiring awe will reign. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/vehu_hayah"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>He was, He is and He will be in glory. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/vehu_echad"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>He is unique and there is no second to compare with Him or to associate with Him. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/beli_reshit"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>Without beginning, without end, to Him might and dominion belong. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/vehu_eli"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>He is my God and my Redeemer lives . </tei:p>
        <tei:p>The rock of my portion in time of distress. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/vehu_nissi"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>He is my banner and a refuge for me, the portion of my cup on the day I call. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/beyado"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>Into His hand I entrust my spirit at the time I sleep and I awake. </tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:adon_olam/veim_ruchi"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n30.jpg" n="4"/>And with my spirit my body. </tei:p>
        <tei:p>God is with me, I do not fear. <tei:milestone unit="stanza"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
